"<h3>Company Payroll Setup</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Short steps, prefilled with what the company already has: canton, UID and the person in charge of the payroll; the rates of the AVS fund, LAA, IJM, LAAC and family allowance policies; the salary rules of the contracts (13th, 14th and 15th salaries and their provision, the value of a vacation day paid at the exit, the flat-rate expenses); the canton's public holidays; how salaries and social charges are booked, on which accounts, and whether the salaries leave the bank as one debit; the salary certificate header. It creates the company's default social insurance configuration. Run it again any time to change a choice."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Configuration de la paie de la société</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Des étapes courtes, préremplies avec ce que la société possède déjà : le canton, le numéro IDE et le responsable des salaires ; les taux de la caisse AVS, de la LAA, de l'IJM, de la LAAC et des allocations familiales ; les règles de salaire des contrats (les 13e, 14e et 15e salaires et leur provision, la valeur d'un jour de vacances versé à la sortie, les frais forfaitaires) ; les jours fériés du canton ; la façon dont les salaires et les charges sociales sont comptabilisés, sur quels comptes, et si les salaires sortent de la banque en un seul débit ; l'en-tête du certificat de salaire. Il crée la configuration des assurances sociales par défaut de la société. Relancez-le à tout moment pour modifier un choix."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Data Import'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/data_import/data_import.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Data Import</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Data import is the tool to migrate your existing data like Employee, Customer, Supplier, and a lot more to our ERPNext system.\n"
"Go through the video for a detailed explanation of this tool."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Import de données</h3>\n"
"\n"
"L'import de données est l'outil pour migrer vos données existantes comme les employés, clients, fournisseurs et bien plus dans notre système ERPNext.\n"
"Regardez la vidéo pour une explication détaillée de cet outil."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Employee'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/create_employee/create_employee.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Employee</h3>\n"
"\n"
"An individual who works and is recognized for his rights and duties in your company is your Employee. You can manage the Employee master. It captures the demographic, personal and professional details, joining and leave details, etc."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Employé</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Un individu qui travaille et est reconnu pour ses droits et devoirs dans votre entreprise est votre employé. Vous pouvez gérer la fiche employé. Elle capture les détails démographiques, personnels et professionnels, les dates d'entrée et de congé, etc."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'HR Settings'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/hr_settings/hr_settings.json
msgid ""
"<h3>HR Settings</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Hr Settings consists of major settings related to Employee Lifecycle, Leave Management, etc. Click on Explore, to explore Hr Settings."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Paramètres RH</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Les paramètres RH regroupent les principaux réglages liés au cycle de vie des employés, à la gestion des congés, etc. Cliquez sur Explorer pour consulter les paramètres RH."

#. Content of the 'Help' (HTML) field in DocType 'Salary Component'
#: hrms/payroll/doctype/salary_component/salary_component.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Help</h3>\n"
"\n"
"<p>Notes:</p>\n"
"\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Use field <code>base</code> for using base salary of the Employee</li>\n"
"<li>Use Salary Component abbreviations in conditions and formulas. <code>BS = Basic Salary</code></li>\n"
"<li>Use field name for employee details in conditions and formulas. <code>Employment Type = employment_type</code><code>Branch = branch</code></li>\n"
"<li>Use field name from Salary Slip in conditions and formulas. <code>Payment Days = payment_days</code><code>Leave without pay = leave_without_pay</code></li>\n"
"<li>Direct Amount can also be entered based on Condition. See example 3</li></ol>\n"
"\n"
"<h4>Examples</h4>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Calculating Basic Salary based on <code>base</code>\n"
"<pre><code>Condition: base &lt; 10000</code></pre>\n"
"<pre><code>Formula: base * .2</code></pre></li>\n"
"<li>Calculating HRA based on Basic Salary<code>BS</code> \n"
"<pre><code>Condition: BS &gt; 2000</code></pre>\n"
"<pre><code>Formula: BS * .1</code></pre></li>\n"
"<li>Calculating TDS based on Employment Type<code>employment_type</code> \n"
"<pre><code>Condition: employment_type==\"Intern\"</code></pre>\n"
"<pre><code>Amount: 1000</code></pre></li>\n"
"</ol>"
msgstr ""
"<h3>Aide</h3>\n"
"\n"
"<p>Notes :</p>\n"
"\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Utilisez le champ <code>base</code> pour utiliser le salaire de base de l'employé</li>\n"
"<li>Utilisez les abréviations des composantes salariales dans les conditions et les formules. <code>BS = Basic Salary</code></li>\n"
"<li>Utilisez le nom du champ pour les détails de l'employé dans les conditions et les formules. <code>Employment Type = employment_type</code><code>Branch = branch</code></li>\n"
"<li>Utilisez le nom du champ du bulletin de salaire dans les conditions et les formules. <code>Payment Days = payment_days</code><code>Leave without pay = leave_without_pay</code></li>\n"
"<li>Le montant direct peut également être saisi en fonction de la condition. Voir l'exemple 3</li></ol>\n"
"\n"
"<h4>Exemples</h4>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Calcul du salaire de base basé sur <code>base</code>\n"
"<pre><code>Condition : base &lt; 10000</code></pre>\n"
"<pre><code>Formule : base * .2</code></pre></li>\n"
"<li>Calcul du HRA basé sur le salaire de base<code>BS</code> \n"
"<pre><code>Condition : BS &gt; 2000</code></pre>\n"
"<pre><code>Formule : BS * .1</code></pre></li>\n"
"<li>Calcul du TDS basé sur le type d'emploi<code>employment_type</code> \n"
"<pre><code>Condition : employment_type==\"Intern\"</code></pre>\n"
"<pre><code>Amount : 1000</code></pre></li>\n"
"</ol>"

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Holiday List'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/create_holiday_list/create_holiday_list.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Holiday List.</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Holiday List is a list which contains the dates of holidays. Most organizations have a standard Holiday List for their employees. However, some of them may have different holiday lists based on different Locations or Departments. In ERPNext, you can configure multiple Holiday Lists."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Liste des jours fériés</h3>\n"
"\n"
"La liste des jours fériés contient les dates de congés. La plupart des organisations ont une liste standard pour leurs employés. Cependant, certaines peuvent avoir des listes différentes selon les sites ou départements. Dans ERPNext, vous pouvez configurer plusieurs listes de jours fériés."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Leave Allocation'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/create_leave_allocation/create_leave_allocation.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Leave Allocation</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Leave Allocation enables you to allocate a specific number of leaves of a particular type to an Employee so that, an employee will be able to create a Leave Application only if Leaves are allocated. "
msgstr ""
"<h3>Attribution de congés</h3>\n"
"\n"
"L'attribution de congés vous permet d'allouer un nombre spécifique de jours d'un type de congé particulier à un employé afin que celui-ci puisse créer une demande de congé uniquement si des jours lui ont été attribués. "

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Leave Application'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/create_leave_application/create_leave_application.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Leave Application</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Leave Application is a formal document created by an Employee to apply for Leaves for a particular time period based on there leave allocation and leave type according to there need."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Demande de congé</h3>\n"
"\n"
"La demande de congé est un document formel créé par un employé pour demander des congés sur une période donnée en fonction de son attribution de congés et du type de congé selon ses besoins."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Leave Type'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/create_leave_type/create_leave_type.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Leave Type</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Leave type is defined based on many factors and features like encashment, earned leaves, partially paid, without pay and, a lot more. To check other options and to define your leave type click on Show Tour."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Type de congé</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Le type de congé est défini en fonction de nombreux facteurs et caractéristiques comme l'encaissement, les congés acquis, partiellement payés, sans solde, et bien plus. Pour vérifier les autres options et définir votre type de congé, cliquez sur Afficher la visite guidée."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Run your first monthly payroll'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/run_your_first_swiss_payroll_cycle/run_your_first_swiss_payroll_cycle.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Monthly Payroll</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Three steps a month: do the payroll (the checks list anything missing, then the slips are generated and submitted), pay the salaries (booked, then a payment proposal for the bank file or EBICS), and hand the payslips out: by e-mail, by post with a WebStamp, or printed."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Paie mensuelle</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Trois étapes par mois : faire la paie (les contrôles listent ce qui manque, puis les fiches sont générées et validées), payer les salaires (comptabilisés, puis une proposition de paiement pour le fichier bancaire ou EBICS), et remettre les fiches de salaire : par e-mail, par la poste avec un WebStamp, ou imprimées."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Assign the salary structure to your
#. employees'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/assign_a_swiss_salary_structure/assign_a_swiss_salary_structure.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Salary Structure Assignment</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Link each employee to the salary structure with their base salary and start date. The monthly cycle only generates slips for employees with a submitted assignment."
msgstr ""

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a salary structure with the Swiss
#. components'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/create_a_swiss_salary_structure/create_a_swiss_salary_structure.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Salary Structure</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Assemble the Swiss components — AVS, AC, LAA, LPP, IJM, source tax — into the structure your employees will be paid with. The Swiss components are created on install; the structure just puts them together."
msgstr ""

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Import the source tax tariffs (ESTV)'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/import_swiss_source_tax_tariffs/import_swiss_source_tax_tariffs.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Source Tax Tariffs (ESTV)</h3>\n"
"\n"
"The official federal tariff files, per canton. Open a tariff of a canton where employees are taxed at source and use Fetch from ESTV to import its brackets. The payroll cycle checks they are present."
msgstr ""
"<h3>Barèmes de l'impôt à la source (ESTV)</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Les fichiers de barèmes fédéraux officiels, par canton. Ouvrez le barème d'un canton où des employés sont imposés à la source et utilisez Récupérer depuis l'ESTV pour importer ses tranches. Le cycle de paie vérifie qu'elles sont présentes."

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Add your first employee (AVS number,
#. permit, source tax)'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/add_your_first_swiss_employee/add_your_first_swiss_employee.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Swiss Employee Wizard</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Five steps: identity, contract, permit, source tax, review. The AVS number is checked as you type, and the source-tax code is suggested from the permit and canton."
msgstr ""

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Set up Swiss payroll (insurances, source
#. tax, first cycle)'
#: hrms/hr/onboarding_step/set_up_swiss_payroll/set_up_swiss_payroll.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Swiss Payroll</h3>\n"
"\n"
"Opens the Swiss payroll workspace: it carries its own checklist — social insurances, source-tax tariffs, salary structure and the first monthly cycle."
msgstr ""

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Configure the Swiss social insurances
#. (AVS, AC, LAA, LPP)'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/configure_swiss_social_insurances/configure_swiss_social_insurances.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Swiss Social Insurances</h3>\n"
"\n"
"AVS, AC, LAA, LPP, IJM and family allowance rates for your company (per canton when needed) — plus the employer IBAN/BIC used to build the salary payment file. One config per company is enough to start."
msgstr ""

#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Review the Swiss wage types catalog'
#: hrms/payroll/onboarding_step/review_swiss_wage_types/review_swiss_wage_types.json
msgid ""
"<h3>Swiss Wage Types</h3>\n"
"\n"
"The catalog of Swissdec wage kinds (base salary, 13th month, source tax…) is seeded on install and drives how each salary component is treated. Review it once — you rarely need to change it."
msgstr ""

#. Content of the 'html_6' (HTML) field in DocType 'Taxable Salary Slab'
#: hrms/payroll/doctype/taxable_salary_slab/taxable_salary_slab.json
msgid ""
"<h4>Condition Examples</h4>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Applying tax if employee born between 31-12-1937 and 01-01-1958 (Employees aged 60 to 80)<br>\n"
"<code>Condition: date_of_birth&gt;date(1937, 12, 31) and date_of_birth&lt;date(1958, 01, 01)</code></li><br><li>Applying tax by employee gender<br>\n"
"<code>Condition: gender==\"Male\"</code></li><br>\n"
"<li>Applying tax by Salary Component<br>\n"
"<code>Condition: base &gt; 10000</code></li></ol>"
msgstr ""
"<h4>Exempleformat@@1\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Appliquer une taxe si un employé né entre 31-12-1937 et 01-01-1958 (Employés âgés de 60 à 80 ans)<br>\n"
"<code>Condition : date_of_birth&gt;date(1937, 12, 31) et date_of_birth&lt;date(1958, 01, 01)</code></li><br><li>Applying tax by employee gender<br>\n"
"<code>Condition: gender==\"Male\"</code></li><br>\n"
"<li>Applying tax by Salary Component<br>\n"
"<code>Condition: base &gt; 10000</code></li></ol>"

